WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.397
The applied challenge combines the module.

00:00:02.397 --> 00:00:04.892
Return one row per admission.

00:00:04.892 --> 00:00:07.727
Create a normalized patient name.

00:00:07.727 --> 00:00:12.967
Extract the email domain while preserving admissions for patients with missing email.

00:00:12.967 --> 00:00:15.532
Create an admission month bucket.

00:00:15.532 --> 00:00:18.112
Add a human-readable admission label.

00:00:18.112 --> 00:00:20.617
Calculate length of stay in hours.

00:00:20.617 --> 00:00:27.097
Build and test one output column at a time instead of trying to finish the entire SELECT immediately.

00:00:27.097 --> 00:00:32.607
Connect this idea to an operations team aligning timestamps across locations.

00:00:32.607 --> 00:00:38.372
Ask what could go wrong if the concept were misunderstood: could rows be duplicated,

00:00:38.372 --> 00:00:45.892
important records disappear, categories be interpreted incorrectly, or a report become difficult to reproduce?

00:00:45.892 --> 00:00:51.897
A strong analyst can explain both the SQL operation and the assumption behind it.

00:00:51.897 --> 00:00:57.737
After the example, summarize the idea in one plain-language sentence before moving on.
